From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nitin Kamboj <nitin.kamboj@amd.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] gst-plugins-base: fix AI layout format bugs, add missing
 RGB/RGBA formats, and rename for consistency (squashed)

Squashed fixup delta against subprojects/gst-plugins-base/ for the AI
layout video format family introduced in commit 938eeb1af3. The base tree
already carries most AI layout formats; this patch corrects bugs found
in that initial landing and registers the remaining missing formats.
Apply from the subprojects/gst-plugins-base/ directory with `patch -p1`.

Part 1 -- Format name consistency fixes
  Three naming inconsistencies in the initial landing are corrected:
  - BGRA8 / BGRA_BF16 / BGRA_FP16 / BGRA_FLOAT renamed to
    BGRA8_C4 / BGRA_BF16_C4 / BGRA_FP16_C4 / BGRA_FLOAT_C4, adding the
    _C4 layout suffix to match the RGBA/RGBX naming convention.
  - RGBX8_C8 / RGBX_BF16_C8 renamed to RGBA8_C8 / RGBA_BF16_C8: these
    formats carry a real alpha channel, not a padding channel, so the 'X'
    designation was wrong.
  - RGBA_FP32_C8 renamed to RGBA_FLOAT_C8, aligning with the FLOAT
    naming convention used throughout the rest of the AI layout family.

Part 2 -- Pack/unpack intermediate format correctness (video-format.c)
  All 16-bit and floating-point AI layout formats had their PACK_ macro
  intermediate format corrected from GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_ARGB (8 bits per
  channel) to GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_ARGB64 (16 bits per channel). Using ARGB
  as the intermediate caused silent truncation of BF16, FP16, and FLOAT
  sample values during pack/unpack. Affected formats: RGBA_BF16_C4,
  RGBA_FP16_C4, RGBA_BF16_C8, RGBA_FP16_C8, BGR_BF16, BGR_FP16,
  BGR_FLOAT, BGR_BF16P, BGR_FP16P, BGRA_BF16P, BGRA_FP16P, and the
  FLOAT_C8 variants.

Part 3 -- Plane-ordering and channel-offset fixes (video-format.c)
  BGR and BGRA planar formats had their GStreamer plane index mapping
  reversed, causing incorrect color output:
  - BGR8P, BGR_BF16P, BGR_FP16P, BGR_FLOATP: PLANE012 -> PLANE210
    (B is byte 0 in memory but maps to plane 2 in GStreamer's RGB-first
    convention).
  - BGRA8P, BGRA_BF16P, BGRA_FP16P, BGRA_FLOATP: PLANE0123 -> PLANE2103
    (matching GStreamer's BGRA planar convention where R->0, G->1, B->2,
    A->3).
  Additionally, the packed BGRA_BF16_C4, BGRA_FP16_C4, and BGRA_FLOAT_C4
  formats had their channel offsets corrected from OFFS2103 to OFFS0123
  (byte order within the interleaved word is BGRA, not RGBA).

Part 4 -- video-converter.c get_scale_format() fix
  GRAY_BF16, GRAY_FP16, and GRAY_FLOAT were mapped to GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_GRAY8
  as their scale format. Corrected to GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_GRAY16_LE, since
  these are 16-bit or wider single-channel formats.

Part 5 -- Add missing formats
  Registers the following formats that were absent from the initial landing,
  with full pack/unpack routines, formats[] table rows, video-info.c
  stride/offset/size, video-converter.c get_scale_format() entries, and
  GST_VIDEO_FORMATS_ALL integration (both BIG_ENDIAN and LITTLE_ENDIAN):
  - GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_RGBA8P: R-first planar 8-bit RGBA (PLANE0123),
    symmetric counterpart to BGRA8P (PLANE2103).
  - GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_BGRX_BF16_C4 / BGRX_FP16_C4: packed 4-channel BGRX
    with BF16 / FP16 per channel (HCWNC4 layout, padding in last channel).
  - GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_RGB_BF16 / RGB_FP16 / RGB_FLOAT: interleaved 3-channel
    RGB at BF16, FP16, and FP32 precision.
  - GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_RGB_BF16P / RGB_FP16P / RGB_FLOATP: planar 3-channel
    RGB at BF16, FP16, and FP32 precision (PLANE012, R-first).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Nitin Kamboj <nitin.kamboj@amd.com>
